                 <h1 class="blog-title">Crack the RRB NTPC Exam 2026: Your Ultimate Guide to Notification, Syllabus &amp; Exam Pattern</h1>
                 <p>Aspiring to join the prestigious Indian Railways? The Railway Recruitment Board (RRB) Non-Technical Popular Categories (NTPC) Exam 2026 presents a golden opportunity for candidates seeking diverse non-technical roles. With the application process recently concluded and exam dates on the horizon, now is the crucial time to solidify your preparation. This comprehensive guide will walk you through the latest notification details, eligibility criteria, the intricate selection process, detailed exam patterns, and the all-important syllabus for the RRB NTPC Exam 2026.</p>

                 <div class="section-title">RRB NTPC 2026 Notification &amp; Key Dates</div>
                 <p>The Railway Recruitment Board has released detailed notifications (CEN 06/2025 for Graduate Level and CEN 07/2025 for Undergraduate Level) for a total of 8868 vacancies for the FY 2025-26, with exams anticipated in 2026. The application process for both graduate and undergraduate level posts has been successfully completed. Candidates are now eagerly awaiting the announcement of the Computer Based Test (CBT) dates. The application status for Graduate Level posts was released on January 20, 2026.</p>
                 <div class="subsection-paragraph benefit-card">
                     <p>✅ A total of 8868 vacancies have been announced for the RRB NTPC 2026 recruitment cycle.</p>
                     <p>✅ The application status for Graduate Level posts was released on January 20, 2026.</p>
                     <p>✅ CBT 1 exams are expected to be conducted in April 2026 for both undergraduate and graduate levels.</p>
                 </div>

