                 <div class="section-title">Eligibility Criteria for RRB NTPC 2026</div>
                 <p>Candidates applying for the RRB NTPC Exam 2026 must meet specific eligibility requirements regarding educational qualification and age limit. The posts are categorized into Graduate and Undergraduate levels.</p>
                 <div class="subsection-paragraph benefit-card">
                     <p>✅ **Educational Qualification:** 12th Pass for Undergraduate level posts and a Graduation Degree from a recognized university for Graduate level posts.</p>
                     <p>✅ **Age Limit:** Minimum 18 years and Maximum 33 years as of January 1, 2026. Age relaxations apply for reserved categories as per government norms.</p>
                 </div>

                 <div class="section-title">RRB NTPC 2026 Selection Process</div>
                 <p>The selection process for the RRB NTPC exam is multi-staged and designed to assess candidates comprehensively. The stages are as follows:</p>

                 <div class="benefit-item">
                   <div class="benefit-title">1. Computer Based Test (CBT) - Stage 1 (Prelims)</div>
                   <div class="benefit-content">This is a qualifying examination. Candidates are shortlisted for CBT 2 based on their normalized scores from CBT 1, approximately 20 times the number of vacancies. All questions are objective type Multiple Choice Questions (MCQs).</div>
                 </div>

                 <div class="benefit-item">
                   <div class="benefit-title">2. Computer Based Test (CBT) - Stage 2 (Mains)</div>
                   <div class="benefit-content">This stage is crucial as the marks obtained here will be considered for the final merit list. It is a screening and scoring round. Candidates must secure higher marks to clear the cut-off for subsequent stages.</div>
                 </div>

                 <div class="benefit-item">
                   <div class="benefit-title">3. Typing Skill Test (TST) / Computer-Based Aptitude Test (CBAT)</div>
                   <div class="benefit-content">Applicable for specific posts. For clerk and typist roles, candidates need to demonstrate a minimum typing speed of 30 words per minute (WPM) in English or 25 WPM in Hindi. For posts like Station Master and Traffic Assistant, a Computer-Based Aptitude Test (CBAT) evaluates concentration, memory, observation, and decision-making abilities.</div>
                 </div>

                 <div class="benefit-item">
                   <div class="benefit-title">4. Document Verification &amp; Medical Examination</div>
                   <div class="benefit-content">Candidates who qualify in all preceding stages undergo document verification, followed by a medical examination as per railway standards.</div>
                 </div>

                 <div class="section-title">RRB NTPC Exam Pattern 2026</div>
                 <p>Understanding the exam pattern is paramount for effective preparation. Both CBT 1 and CBT 2 consist of objective-type questions with negative marking.</p>

