                 <div class="section-title">Comprehensive RRB NTPC Syllabus 2026</div>
                 <p>The syllabus for both CBT 1 and CBT 2 largely remains the same, covering General Awareness, Mathematics, and General Intelligence &amp; Reasoning. However, the depth and number of questions vary.</p>

                 <div class="benefit-item">
                   <div class="benefit-title">1. General Awareness (GA)</div>
                   <div class="benefit-content">
                       <p>This section is highly weighted and can be a game-changer. Topics include: Current Events of National and International Importance, Games and Sports, Art and Culture of India, Indian Literature, Monuments and Places of India, General Science and Life Science (up to 10th CBSE), History of India and Freedom Struggle, Physical, Social and Economic Geography of India and World, Indian Polity and Governance (constitution and political system), General Scientific and Technological Developments (Space and Nuclear Program of India), UN and Other Important World Organizations, Common Abbreviations, Transport Systems in India, Indian Economy, Basics of Computers and Computer Applications, Environmental Issues, Famous Personalities.</p>
                   </div>
                 </div>

                 <div class="benefit-item">
                   <div class="benefit-title">2. Mathematics</div>
                   <div class="benefit-content">
                       <p>Focus on foundational concepts and problem-solving. Key topics: Number System, Decimals, Fractions, LCM, HCF, Ratio and Proportions, Percentages, Mensuration, Time and Work, Time and Distance, Simple and Compound Interest, Profit and Loss, Elementary Algebra, Geometry and Trigonometry, Elementary Statistics.</p>
                   </div>
                 </div>

                 <div class="benefit-item">
                   <div class="benefit-title">3. General Intelligence &amp; Reasoning</div>
                   <div class="benefit-content">
                       <p>This section tests your logical and analytical abilities. Important topics: Analogies, Completion of Number and Alphabetical Series, Coding and Decoding, Mathematical Operations, Similarities and Differences, Relationships (Blood Relations), Analytical Reasoning (including Syllogism, Jumbling), Venn Diagrams, Puzzle, Seating Arrangement, Direction and Distance, Data Sufficiency, Statement-Conclusion/Assumptions.</p>
                   </div>
                 </div>

                 <div class="highlight-text">
                     <p>💡 Pro Tip: The syllabus for CBT 1 and CBT 2 remains largely the same, but the number of questions and marks differ. Focus on consistent practice and in-depth understanding for both stages.</p>
                 </div>

                 <div class="section-title">Preparation Strategy &amp; Conclusion</div>
                 <p>With the RRB NTPC Exam 2026 dates drawing near, a well-structured preparation strategy is indispensable. Dedicate sufficient time to each section, focusing on high-weightage topics in General Awareness, and consistent practice for Mathematics and Reasoning. Attempting mock tests regularly will help you identify your strengths and weaknesses, improve time management, and familiarize yourself with the exam environment. Stay updated with current affairs and refer to previous year's papers for better insights. Your dedication and smart preparation will undoubtedly pave the way for a successful career in the Indian Railways!</p>
